d_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Discussed in https://github.com/sqlalchemy/sqlalchemy/discussions/9360\r\n\r\nI looked through automap and in no place does it create inheriting classes, so for the next five minutes until I see where this goes wrong, let's enjoy a totally impossible paradox of a test case\r\n\r\n```py\r\nfrom sqlalchemy import Column\r\nfrom sqlalchemy import create_engine\r\nfrom sqlalchemy import Integer\r\nfrom sqlalchemy.ext.automap import automap_base\r\n\r\nengine = create_engine('sqlite://', echo=True)\r\n\r\nBase = automap_base()\r\n\r\nclass TestData(Base):\r\n    __tablename__ = 'testdata'\r\n    id = Column('id',Integer,autoincrement=True, primary_key=True)\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nclass TestUser(Base):\r\n    __tablename__ = 'testuser'\r\n    id = Column('id',Integer,autoincrement=True, primary_key=True)\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nTestData.metadata.create_all(engine)\r\nTestData.prepare(engine)\r\n\r\nTestUser.metadata.create_all(engine)\r\nTestUser.prepare(engine)\r\n\r\n\r\n```\r\n\r\nit seems to want to find a foreign key between these two and in later 1.4 versions ends up with\r\n\r\n```\r\nsqlalchemy.exc.NoForeignKeysError: Can't determine the inherit condition between inherited table 'testdata' and inheriting table 'testuser'; tables have no foreign key relationships established.  Please ensure the inheriting table has a foreign key relationship to the inherited table, or provide an 'on clause' using the 'inherit_condition' mapper argument.\r\n\r\n```\r\n\r\nIn earlier versions it crashes on trying to find FKs between the two classes.  issue is on 2.0 as well (!!!!) even after we made some improvements to automap in #5145 which explicitly allows multiple prepare() calls.\r\n\r\nthe issue seems to be related to calling prepare() from the mapped class and not the base.\r\n\r\n\r\n","closed_by":{"login":"sqlalchemy-bot","id":36047385,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM2MDQ3Mzg1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubuserconten